<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kazakh ASSR</h1><p class="st-meta">1920 CE – 1936 CE · capital Orenburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The autonomous Soviet republic of the Kazakhs within Russia, whose collectivisation brought a famine that killed over a third of the Kazakh people.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In August 1920 the Soviet government created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kirghiz-assr">Kirghiz ASSR</a>, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakhs</a> were then called by Russians, within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orenburg">Orenburg</a> as capital, absorbing the territory of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/alash-autonomy">Alash Autonomy</a>. In 1925 it was renamed the Kazakh ASSR, the capital moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyzylorda">Kyzylorda</a>, and in 1929 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almaty">Alma-Ata</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic's leaders, such as First Secretary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/filipp-goloshchekin">Filipp Goloshchekin</a> from 1925, imposed Soviet rule on a mainly nomadic population. Collectivisation and forced settlement of nomads from 1929, combined with grain and livestock requisitioning, caused the famine of 1930 to 1933, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakh-famine-of-1930-1933">Asharshylyk</a>, in which about 1.5 million people died and many fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the 1936 Soviet constitution the republic was raised to the status of a union republic, becoming the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kazakh-ssr">Kazakh SSR</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kazakh-assr.jpg" alt="Kazakh ASSR" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Tohaomg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_The_Kazakh_Autonomous_Socialist_Soviet_Republic_(1920-36).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1920 CE – 1936 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Orenburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Filipp Goloshchekin, Levon Mirzoyan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kazakh, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Kazakhstan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kirghiz ASSR (1920-1925), Kazak ASSR</dd></dl></aside></div>
